historicalRank":{"fieldSizeRank":6,"finishersRank":3,"finishRateRank":84,"winningTimeRank":7,"winningTimeRankDir":2,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"womenRecords":["up"],"womenPreviousRecord":{"time":"05:58:53","holder":"Gerda STEYN","year":2019,"type":"up"},"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1975,"mensWinner":"Derek PREISS","mensTime":"05:53:00"}},"narrative":"The 2024 Comrades Marathon was the 97th running of the race, run in the 'up' direction from Durban to Pietermaritzburg.\n\nPiet WIERSMA claimed the men's title in 05:25:00, ahead of Dan MOSELAKWE (05:25:45) and Degefa Yohannese LAFEBO (05:27:48). Gerda STEYN won the women's race in 05:49:46, followed by Alexandra MOROZOVA (06:05:12).\n\nGerda STEYN's 05:49:46 broke her own women's up record of 05:58:53 from 2019. Gerda STEYN's 05:49:46 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1975 (Derek PREISS, 05:53:00).\n\nFrom a field of 22,516 entries, 17,305 runners crossed the finish line (76.9% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 14,006 men and 3,295 women (19.0% female). The average finish time was 10:13:22.\n\nMedals awarded: 20 Gold, 31 Wally Hayward, 805 Silver, 6,095 Bill Rowan, 4,452 Bronze, 5,902 Vic Clapham. 4,308 runners (24.9%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Eddie MKHABELE in 12:00:00.\n\nThis edition featured the 3rd most finishers ever. Compared to the previous up run in 2019, the field was 8.6% smaller.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 69% of the finishers, with 5,270 seniors (avg 09:55:58) and 11,899 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}